# Evidence dashboard — Supabase Postgres source.
# Copy to `dashboard/.env` (gitignored) and fill in the real password.
#
# Evidence loads the `supabase` source (dashboard/sources/supabase/connection.yaml)
# from this env var. The var name encodes the source name:
#   EVIDENCE_SOURCE__<source name>__<option>
# We pass a full connectionString rather than discrete host/port/user/pass.
#
# Project: zcjbtpxuhdekpwcxmepn
#
# IMPORTANT — pick the right host:
#   * Direct (db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432) is IPv6-only on Supabase. It works from
#     IPv6-capable machines but FAILS from most CI / Evidence Cloud (IPv4-only).
#   * Session pooler (aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432) is IPv4 and is the
#     right choice for Evidence Cloud and GitHub Actions builds. Note the user is
#     "postgres.<ref>" for the pooler, not plain "postgres".
#
# Direct (local, IPv6):
# EVIDENCE_SOURCE__supabase__connectionString=postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.zcjbtpxuhdekpwcxmepn.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Session pooler (CI / Evidence Cloud / IPv4) — recommended:
EVIDENCE_SOURCE__supabase__connectionString=postgresql://postgres.zcjbtpxuhdekpwcxmepn:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
